sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-024-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) spicule rays as Plateau borders of the secreting cell field vs Grantia SEM ray angles (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 62.3/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Neumann tension triangle (E1-E3) with the equiangular point (E4), the one-parameter sagittal family cos(theta_pair) = -rho/2 (E5), tetrahedral/orthogonal limits (E7/E8) and the curvilinear interstice (E9); six Lean theorems kernel-checked. Radial-arc ray extraction on the SEM plate finds 8 three-ray spicules and 3 monaxons (self-tested). Angles: all-angle SD 15.5 deg; closest-pair difference median 4.2 deg (mean 5.7); unpaired deviation mean 27.0 deg; ratio 4.7; fitted rho spans 0.37 (T-shaped atrial tetractine) to 1.43 (Y-shaped cortical triactine); 3/8 spicules equiangular within 10 deg. Verdict is withheld until Pass 2 adds a null control: in Pass 1 the small paired difference has no reference distribution. Overall (weighted) 62.3/100. Overall 62.3/100 (faithfulness 58.0, reproducibility 72.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 45, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 66. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_024_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-024_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py at 0643f406e28a6ba3f9600caef4642142fc8be064, image/png, 324123 B, 1870×792 px, artifact_sha256 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc (sha256 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc), spec_fingerprint 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 77e8201d27dd51cb520268fe921b47c6a9cc21b65c7f28e750eaa978978c6f12; artifact_sha256: 3f92607c5d3f21ac06d4baaf5982288625f9ce76cc2ef37224d4943b1763e6fc; input_dataset_sha256: {dryad_8mv00jv_dataset_metadata.json=8b1273b453ccdb77..., grantia_indica_zootaxa4426_fig53_sem.jpg=70194abe78894820..., grantia_spicules_readey_100x.jpg=08641621770534e1..., thompson1917_fig214_ia_leaf465_p445.jpg=019168c1fa4adddc...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917, pp. 443-449) argues, after Dreyer (1892) and Plateau (1873), that calcareous spicule rays follow the junction lines of 3 or 4 contiguous cells: 120 deg when tensions are equal, 'two equal angles and one unequal' when not, tetrahedral ~109 deg for four cells; the spicule is 'a crystal under restraint'. | Thompson gives drawings (Fig. 214, after Haeckel) and no measured angle table.; reconstructed_in_script: Neumann law of cosines in integer-exact form (E3), sagittal one-parameter family (E5) and its inverse, tetrahedral/orthogonal constants, radial-arc ray-angle extraction on one CC BY SEM plate of Grantia aff. indica (8 three-ray spicules, 3 monaxons), per-spicule rho fit, side-by-side renders, layered growth animation.; transfer_boundary: One plate, one individual, one genus; 2D projection of trihedral spicules; tetractine apical ray not measurable (P3 untestable here); no alcyonarian spicules at all although the claim text names them.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the mechanism (passive deposition between arbitrary neighbouring cells) is correct: Ledger & Jones (1977) and Voigt et al. (2017) show a dedicated sclerocyte sextet; only the geometric content (ray axes obey a tension-triangle force balance of the secreting cell group) is tested. | Does NOT claim a verdict in Pass 1: the paired-difference statistic has no null distribution yet (R2). | Does NOT use the pre-assigned Dryad dataset (hexactine fossil tomograms, 5.8 GB): recorded as DATASET_MISMATCH, metadata pinned.." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"Null control for the paired-difference statistic: Monte Carlo Dirichlet(1,1,1) random partitions of 360 deg (smallest-gap distribution) with a one-sided p-value and KS test; otherwise 'two equal angles' is unsupported\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Parameter sweep: rho from 0 to 2 with measured outputs (angle triplets re-measured from rendered spicules by the same radial method — closes the measurement loop) and the general three-tension model'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': \"Second specimen population: segment the CC BY-SA Grantia micrograph (many free triradiates) for the P1 120-deg mode, and digitise Thompson's own Fig. 214 (pinned IA leaf 465) with the same method\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Goodness-of-fit: Pearson r and RMSE of model-predicted vs measured angle triplets, CV of angles, near-axis vs chord-axis sensitivity'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Fix the basal-ray orientation heuristic for rho > 1 spicules and render the tetractine apical ray / ray curvature honestly (or state the limit)'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': \"Ablation control: a 'crystallographic' alternative (Haeckel's view Thompson argues against — discrete 60/90/120 deg axes) vs the continuous E5 family, scored on the same data\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'Expose rho, threshold and radial parameters on the CLI; silence/upgrade the scikit-image deprecations'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.623"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1; second assessor pending)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 .
}

